# Environment Variable Configuration Example

# ============================================
# FRONTEND (Vercel)
# ============================================

# Backend API URL - REQUIRED for frontend to connect to backend
# This MUST be set in Vercel dashboard under Settings → Environment Variables

VITE_API_URL=https://fake-identity-screening.onrender.com

# ============================================
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# ============================================

# For local testing, create frontend/.env.local with:
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:10000

# ============================================
# IMPORTANT NOTES
# ============================================

# 1. Variable name MUST start with VITE_ for Vite to include it
# 2. Vercel requires redeploy after adding environment variables
# 3. Backend URL must include https:// protocol
# 4. No trailing slash in URL

# ============================================
# HOW TO SET IN VERCEL
# ============================================

# Option 1: Dashboard
# 1. Go to vercel.com → Your Project → Settings
# 2. Click "Environment Variables"
# 3. Add: VITE_API_URL = https://fake-identity-screening.onrender.com
# 4. Check: Production, Preview, Development
# 5. Save and redeploy

# Option 2: CLI
# vercel env add VITE_API_URL
# Enter value when prompted
# Then: vercel --prod

# ============================================
# VERIFICATION
# ============================================

# After deployment, check in browser console:
# console.log(import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL)
# Should output: https://fake-identity-screening.onrender.com
